{
  "case_id": "2022-21-887",
  "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument this morning in Case 21-887, Perez versus Sturgis Public Schools. Mr. Martinez."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Sturgis wants you to hold that this settlement extinguishes Miguel's separate and distinct rights to money damages under the ADA. You should reject that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "First, the text only requires exhaustion if a non-IDEA claim seeks relief that's actually available under the IDEA. Exhaustion isn't required in cases like this one seeking only money damages, a remedy the IDEA does not authorize."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: If the -- this -- if this statute were written in a way that you had a progression of remedies from administrative, from informal to formal, and it was about the very same thing, that is, the education of Petitioner, then why -- then wouldn't this be exhausted at some level?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Martinez",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think -- I think your point about how the settlement negotiations would play out is extremely important, and I think it favors us because what -- our rule would allow the parties to come together. If they can reach a global settlement of everything, terrific. But, if they can only reach a partial settlement, if they can only reach a settlement that addresses the IDEA claims, our rule would say, yes, of course, in that case, the student and the parents should accept that settlement, get the on-the-ground FAPE relief immediately, and then the parties can agree to go on and fight about the ADA claims for relief later."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Martinez",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "you -- if you're not willing to give up the ADA claims, you get -- you can't get anything by settlement because the -- the effect of the settlement is to give up everything. That rule doesn't make sense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Under Fry, is the gravamen of Petitioner's complaint the denial of a FAPE?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If the -- suppose there were no IDEA. Could Petitioner prevail on a straight ADA claim? And, if so, what would be the nature of the --of the claim?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When -- when you said before, Mr. Yang, that the Court should decide the antecedent question first, the logically antecedent question, is there any other reason than, oh, it's logically antecedent that you would rather have us decide that question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Yang",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. YANG: I mean, there's just nothing to do. What would happen here is exactly what happened here, which is that the hearing officer dismisses the ADA claim --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dvoretzky",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 51,
        "start": 51
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When Congress enacted Section 1415(l), it channeled all FAPE denial claims through the IDEA's exhaustion procedures. Congress carefully crafted those procedures, and it wanted parents and school districts to go through them because of the primacy of a FAPE."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0002-0006",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the reason for that is because of the primacy of getting a FAPE under the IDEA. The exhaustion requirement is designed to say, you can pursue your other claims later, but, first and foremost, you have to try to get a FAPE because that's what's in the best interests of the child."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Which of the two default rules better serves the objectives of the IDEA?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dvoretzky",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't think the Court would likely find that the exhaustion requirement is a jurisdictional one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, absent waiver by the other side, it would operate in the way Mr. Martinez suggests, wouldn't it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0003-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 86,
        "start": 86
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what about Mr. Yang's point that the majority rule in the circuits is that the futility exception applies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Can you think of any claim in the context of this case that could have been brought under ADA that need not have been exhausted?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 88,
        "start": 88
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: I -- I do want to just ask you one more question about the relief point because it seems like you spent most of your time elsewhere, understandably. The text says \"relief that is also available under this subchapter.\" I mean, just focus with me for a second on just those words."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Roman Martinez (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-887",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05ebdebb8d96d4639a893030ed0dd2fc8ffa1cccbfca48ad088adadc79dde28b",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05ebdebb8d96-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 97,
        "start": 97
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF ROMAN MARTINEZ ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER MR. MARTINEZ: Your Honors, I think Sturgis's answer to Justice Kagan's question about Miguel's dilemma really gives away the game here. Their answer is that if Sturgis had refused to cave in, had refused to give Miguel more than it had already negotiated, Miguel would have had to reject the settlement, turn down the immediate FAPE relief, and roll the dice in an IDEA proceeding that might risk not only his recovery but also his attorneys' fees."
    },
    {
